        "text": "Next, let's get into the basics of swing trading. It has some similarities with day trading but works on a longer time frame. Positions are usually held anywhere from a couple of days to a couple of months. The goal here is to profit from larger swings in price. Your goal as a swing trader is to identify assets that could be undervalued and are likely to increase in price. In this case, you would purchase this asset and sell it when the price rises to generate a profit. The opposite trade looks to profit from downward price swings. If your analysis tells you that a bear market for gold might be coming to an end, you could purchase gold in anticipation of rising future prices. However, the transition between a bear and bull market can take place over months. In this case, you purchase gold now, waiting for the price to increase in the next one to two months. If the price does rise, you sell off the asset and take home your profit.",
